H7600.definition:
from H7599 (שָׁאַן);
secure; in a bad sense, haughty
KJV: that is at ease, quiet, tumult. Compare H7946 (שַׁלְאֲנָן).

H7601.definition:
a primitive root;
to plunder
KJV: spoil.

H7602.definition:
a primitive root;
to inhale eagerly; figuratively, to cover; by implication, to be angry; also to hasten
KJV: desire (earnestly), devour, haste, pant, snuff up, swallow up.

H7603.definition:
from H7604 (שָׁאַר);
barm or yeast-cake (as swelling by fermentation)
KJV: leaven.

H7604.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to swell up, i.e. be (causatively, make) redundant
KJV: leave, (be) left, let, remain, remnant, reserve, the rest.

H7605.definition:
from H7604 (שָׁאַר);
a remainder
KJV: [idiom] other, remnant, residue, rest.

H7606.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7605 (שְׁאָר)
{a remainder}
KJV: [idiom] whatsoever more, residue, rest.

H7607.definition:
from H7604 (שָׁאַר);
flesh (as swelling out), as living or forfood; generally food of any kind; figuratively, kindred by blood
KJV: body, flesh, food, (near) kin(-sman, -swoman), near (nigh) (of kin).

H7608.definition:
feminine of H7607 (שְׁאֵר);
female kindred by blood
KJV: near kinswomen.

H7609.definition:
the same as H7608 (שַׁאֲרָה);
Sheerah, an Israelitess
KJV: Sherah.

H7610.definition:
from H7605 (שְׁאָר) and H7725 (שׁוּב); a remnant will return;
Shear-Jashub, the symbolic name of one of Isaiah's sons
KJV: Shear-jashub.

H7611.definition:
from H7604 (שָׁאַר);
a remainder or residual (surviving, final) portion
KJV: that had escaped, be left, posterity, remain(-der), remnant, residue, rest.

H7613.definition:
from H5375 (נָשָׂא);
an elevation or leprous scab; figuratively, elation or cheerfulness; exaltation in rank or character
KJV: be accepted, dignity, excellency, highness, raise up self, rising.

H7614.definition:
of foreign origin;
Sheba, the name of three early progenitors of tribes and of an Ethiopian district
KJV: Sheba, Sabeans.

H7615.definition:
patronymic from H7614 (שְׁבָא);
a Shebaite or descendant of Sheba
KJV: Sabean.

H7616.definition:
from an unused root meaning to break up;
a fragment, i.e. ruin
KJV: broken in pieces.

H7617.definition:
a primitive root;
to transport into captivity
KJV: (bring away, carry, carry away, lead, lead away, take) captive(-s), drive (take) away.

H7618.definition:
from an unused root (probably identical with that of H7617 (שָׁבָה) through the idea of subdivision into flashes or streamers (compare H7632 (שָׁבִיב)) meaning to flame;
a gem (from its sparkle), probably the agate
KJV: agate.

H7619.definition:
or שׁוּבָאֵל; from H7617 (שָׁבָה) (abbreviated form) or H7725 (שׁוּב) and H410 (אֵל); captive (or returned) of God;
Shebuel or Shubael, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Shebuel, Shubael.

H7620.definition:
or שָׁבֻעַ; also (feminine) שְׁבֻעָה; properly, passive participle of H7650 (שָׁבַע) as a denominative of H7651 (שֶׁבַע);
literally, sevened, i.e. a week (specifically, of years)
KJV: seven, week.

H7621.definition:
feminine passive participle of H7650 (שָׁבַע);
properly, something sworn, i.e. an oath
KJV: curse, oath, [idiom] sworn.

H7622.definition:
or שְׁבִית; from H7617 (שָׁבָה);
exile, concretely, prisoners; figuratively, a former state of prosperity
KJV: captive(-ity).

H7623.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to address in aloud tone, i.e. (specifically) loud; figuratively, to pacify (as if by words)
KJV: commend, glory, keep in, praise, still, triumph.

H7624.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7623 (שָׁבַח);
to adulate, i.e. adore
KJV: praise.

H7625.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7626 (שֵׁבֶט);
a clan
KJV: tribe.

H7626.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to branch off;
a scion, i.e. (literally) a stick (for punishing, writing, fighting, ruling, walking, etc.) or (figuratively) a clan
KJV: [idiom] correction, dart, rod, sceptre, staff, tribe.

H7627.definition:
of foreign origin;
Shebat, a Jewish month
KJV: Sebat.

H7628.definition:
from H7618 (שְׁבוּ);
exiled; captured; as noun, exile (abstractly or concretely and collectively); by extension, booty
KJV: captive(-ity), prisoners, [idiom] take away, that was taken.

H7629.definition:
from H7617 (שָׁבָה); captor;
Shobi, an Ammonite
KJV: Shobi.

H7630.definition:
for H7629 (שֹׁבִי);
Shobai, an Israelite
KJV: Shobai.

H7631.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7632 (שָׁבִיב)
{flame (as split into tongues)}
KJV: flame.

H7632.definition:
from the same as H7616 (שָׁבָב);
flame (as split into tongues)
KJV: spark.

H7633.definition:
feminine of H7628 (שְׁבִי);
exile (abstractly or concretely and collectively)
KJV: captives(-ity).

H7634.definition:
feminine of the same as H7629 (שֹׁבִי); captivation;
Shobjah, an Israelite
KJV: Shachia (from the margin).

H7635.definition:
from the same as H7640 (שֹׁבֶל);
a track or passage-way (as if flowing along)
KJV: path.

H7636.definition:
from an unused root meaning to interweave;
a netting for the hair
KJV: caul.

H7637.definition:
or שְׁבִעִי; ordinal from H7657 (שִׁבְעִים);
seventh
KJV: seventh (time).

H7638.definition:
from an unused root meaning to intwine;
a netting (ornament to the capital of a column)
KJV: net.

H7639.definition:
feminine of H7638 (שָׂבָךְ);
a net-work, i.e. (in hunting) a snare, (in architecture) a ballustrade; also a reticulated ornament to apillar
KJV: checker, lattice, network, snare, wreath(-enwork).

H7640.definition:
from an unused root meaning to flow;
a lady's train (as trailing after her)
KJV: leg.

H7641.definition:
or (feminine) שִׁבֹּלֶת; from the same as H7640 (שֹׁבֶל);
a stream (as flowing); also an ear of grain (as growing out); by analogy, a branch
KJV: branch, channel, ear (of corn), (water-)flood, Shibboleth. Compare H5451 (סִבֹּלֶת).

H7642.definition:
from the same as H7640 (שֹׁבֶל);
a snail (as if floating in its own slime)
KJV: snail.

H7643.definition:
or (feminine) שִׂבְמָה; probably from H1313 (בָּשָׂם); spice;
Sebam or Sibmah, a place in Moab
KJV: Shebam, Shibmah, Sibmah.

H7644.definition:
or שֶׁבְנָה; from an unused root meaning to grow; growth;
Shebna or Shebnah, an Israelite
KJV: Shebna, Shebnah.

H7645.definition:
or שְׁבַנְיָהוּ; from the same as H7644 (שֶׁבְנָא) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has grown (i.e. prospered);
Shebanjah, the name of three or four Israelites
KJV: Shebaniah.

H7646.definition:
or שָׂבֵעַ; a primitive root;
to sate, i.e. fill to satisfaction (literally or figuratively)
KJV: have enough, fill (full, self, with), be (to the) full (of), have plenty of, be satiate, satisfy (with), suffice, be weary of.

H7647.definition:
from H7646 (שָׂבַע);
copiousness
KJV: abundance, plenteous(-ness, -ly).

H7648.definition:
from H7646 (שָׂבַע);
satisfaction (of food or (figuratively) joy)
KJV: fill, full(-ness), satisfying, be satisfied.

H7649.definition:
from H7646 (שָׂבַע);
satiated (in a pleasant or disagreeable sense)
KJV: full (of), satisfied (with).

H7650.definition:
a primitive root; properly to be complete, but used only as a denominative from H7651 (שֶׁבַע);
to seven oneself, i.e. swear (as if by repeating a declaration seven times)
KJV: adjure, charge (by an oath, with an oath), feed to the full (by mistake for H7646 (שָׂבַע)), take an oath, [idiom] straitly, (cause to, make to) swear.

H7651.definition:
or (masculine) (שִׁבְעָה); from H7650 (שָׁבַע); a primitive cardinal number;
seven (as the sacred full one); also (adverbially) seven times; by implication, a week; by extension, an indefinite number
KJV: ([phrase] by) seven(-fold),-s, (-teen, -teenth), -th, times). Compare H7658 (שִׁבְעָנָה).

H7652.definition:
the same as H7651 (שֶׁבַע); seven;
Sheba, the name of a place in Palestine, and of two Israelites
KJV: Sheba.

H7653.definition:
feminine of H7647 (שָׂבָע);
satiety
KJV: fulness.

H7654.definition:
feminine of H7648 (שֹׂבַע);
satiety
KJV: (to have) enough, [idiom] till...be full, (un-) satiable, satisfy, [idiom] sufficiently.

H7655.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7651 (שֶׁבַע)
{seven (as the sacred full one); also (adverbially) seven times; by implication, a week; by extension, an indefinite number}
KJV: seven (times).

H7656.definition:
masculine of H7651 (שֶׁבַע); seven(-th);
Shebah, a well in Palestine
KJV: Shebah.

H7657.definition:
multiple of H7651 (שֶׁבַע);
seventy
KJV: seventy, threescore and ten ([phrase] -teen).

H7658.definition:
prolonged for the masculine of H7651 (שֶׁבַע);
seven
KJV: seven.

H7659.definition:
dual (adverbially) of H7651 (שֶׁבַע);
seven-times
KJV: seven(-fold, times).

H7660.definition:
a primitive root;
to interweave (colored) threads in squares; by implication (of reticulation) to inchase gems in gold
KJV: embroider, set.

H7661.definition:
from H7660 (שָׁבַץ);
entanglement, i.e. (figuratively) perplexity
KJV: anguish.

H7662.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to the root of H7733 (שׁוֹבֵק);
to quit, i.e. allow to remain
KJV: leave, let alone.

H7663.definition:
erroneously שָׁבַר; (Nehemiah 2:13,15), a primitive root;
to scrutinize; by implication (of watching) to expect (with hope and patience)
KJV: hope, tarry, view, wait.

H7665.definition:
a primitive root;
to burst (literally or figuratively)
KJV: break (down, off, in pieces, up), broken (-hearted), bring to the birth, crush, destroy, hurt, quench, [idiom] quite, tear, view (by mistake for H7663 (שָׂבַר)).

H7666.definition:
denominative from H7668 (שֶׁבֶר);
to deal in grain
KJV: buy, sell.

H7667.definition:
or שֵׁבֶר; from H7665 (שָׁבַר);
a fracture, figuratively, ruin; specifically, a solution (of a dream)
KJV: affliction, breach, breaking, broken(-footed, -handed), bruise, crashing, destruction, hurt, interpretation, vexation.

H7668.definition:
the same as H7667 (שֶׁבֶר);
grain (as if broken into kernels)
KJV: corn, victuals.

H7669.definition:
the same as H7667 (שֶׁבֶר);
Sheber, an Israelite
KJV: Sheber.

H7670.definition:
from H7665 (שָׁבַר);
rupture, i.e. a pang; figuratively, ruin
KJV: breaking, destruction.

H7671.definition:
plural of H7667 (שֶׁבֶר); ruins;
Shebarim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Shebarim.

H7672.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7660 (שָׁבַץ);
to entangle, i.e. perplex
KJV: be astonished.

H7673.definition:
a primitive root;
to repose, i.e. desist from exertion; used in many implied relations (causative, figurative or specific)
KJV: (cause to, let, make to) cease, celebrate, cause (make) to fail, keep (sabbath), suffer to be lacking, leave, put away (down), (make to) rest, rid, still, take away.

H7674.definition:
from H7673 (שָׁבַת);
rest, interruption, cessation
KJV: cease, sit still, loss of time.

H7675.definition:
infinitive of H3427 (יָשַׁב);
properly, session; but used also concretely, an abode or locality
KJV: place, seat. Compare H3429 (יֹשֵׁב בַּשֶּׁבֶת).

H7676.definition:
intensive from H7673 (שָׁבַת);
intermission, i.e (specifically) the Sabbath
KJV: ([phrase] every) sabbath.

H7677.definition:
from H7676 (שַׁבָּת);
a sabbatism or special holiday
KJV: rest, sabbath.

H7678.definition:
from H7676 (שַׁבָּת); restful;
Shabbethai, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Shabbethai.

H7679.definition:
; a primitive root;
to grow, i.e. (causatively) to enlarge, (figuratively) laud
KJV: increase, magnify.

H7680.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7679 (שָׂגָא);
to increase
KJV: grow, be multiplied.

H7681.definition:
probably from H7686 (שָׁגָה); erring;
Shage, an Israelite
KJV: Shage.

H7682.definition:
a primitive root;
to be (causatively, make) lofty, especially inaccessible; by implication, safe, strong; used literally and figuratively
KJV: defend, exalt, be excellent, (be, set on) high, lofty, be safe, set up (on high), be too strong.

H7683.definition:
a primitive root;
to stray, i.e. (figuratively) sin (with more or less apology)
KJV: [idiom] also for that, deceived, err, go astray, sin ignorantly.

H7684.definition:
from H7683 (שָׁגַג);
a mistake or inadvertent transgression
KJV: error, ignorance, at unawares; unwittingly.

H7685.definition:
a primitive root;
to enlarge (especially upward, also figuratively)
KJV: grow (up), increase.

H7686.definition:
a primitive root;
to stray (causatively, mislead), usually (figuratively) to mistake, especially (morally) to transgress; by extension (through the idea of intoxication) to reel, (figuratively) be enraptured
KJV: (cause to) go astray, deceive, err, be ravished, sin through ignorance, (let, make to) wander.

H7687.definition:
from H7682 (שָׂגַב); aloft;
Segub, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Segub.

H7688.definition:
a primitive root;
to peep, i.e. glance sharply at
KJV: look (narrowly).

H7689.definition:
from H7679 (שָׂגָא);
(superlatively) mighty
KJV: excellent, great.

H7690.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7689 (שַׂגִּיא);
large (in size, quantity or number, also adverbial)
KJV: exceeding, great(-ly); many, much, sore, very.

H7691.definition:
from H7686 (שָׁגָה);
a moral mistake
KJV: error.

H7692.definition:
or שִׁגָּיֹנָה; from H7686 (שָׁגָה);
properly, aberration, i.e. (technically) a dithyramb or rambling poem
KJV: Shiggaion, Shigionoth.

H7693.definition:
a primitive root;
to copulate with
KJV: lie with, ravish.

H7694.definition:
from H7693 (שָׁגַל);
a queen (from cohabitation)
KJV: queen.

H7695.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7694 (שֵׁגָל);
a (legitimate) queen
KJV: wife.

H7696.definition:
a primitive root;
to rave through insanity
KJV: (be, play the) mad (man).

H7697.definition:
from H7696 (שָׁגַע);
craziness
KJV: furiously, madness.

H7698.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to eject;
the fetus (as finally expelled)
KJV: that cometh of, increase.

H7699.definition:
or שֹׁד; probably from H7736 (שׁוּד) (in its original sense) contracted;
the breast of a woman or animal (as bulging)
KJV: breast, pap, teat.
